src.tar.Z contains the source patches of the 
first 1.5 AmigaMINIX update, as well as a new
/dev/Makedev and /bin/format.

You can install it by transferring the compressed tarfile to
minix (using the minix transfer utility on the AmigaDOS side
and on the minix side.)
There you can decompress and untar it onto an empty floppy.
When trying to apply the patches you can run out of memory,
both on the root filesystem and in patch itself.  The first
problem can be solved by removing most or all of the binaries
from /bin, or by using a larger ram disk/root filesystem.
The second problem can be solved by giving patch more stack
space, with chmem (64 kb should probably be enough.)
